    "text": "Rory McIlroy's wife, Erica, was reportedly wearing a $100,000 ensemble at The Masters on Sunday.Erica Stoll, who married Rory McIlroy in 2017, was spotted in a tan dress, white flowing dress and luxury watch as her husband won The Masters for the second straight year. The ensemble is estimated to cost more than $100,000, with the luxury watch taking up most of that cost.McIlroy, who is worth more than $500 million, according to industry experts, can certainly afford that kind of outfit price for his wife. He just won $4.5 million for taking home The Masters' title, too.Apr 8, 2026; Augusta, Georgia, USA; Rory McIlroy leans in to kiss his wife, Erica Stoll, on the ninth green during the Par 3 Contest at the Masters Tournament at Augusta National Golf Club. Mandatory Credit: Kyle Terada-Imagn Images© Kyle Terada-Imagn Images.Erica was spotted wearing a Patek Phillipe Twenty-4 in rolls gold, which can go for as much as six figures. Her dress, hat and shoes likely added a few thousand to the price tag. In total, Erica Stoll was rocking more than $100,000 worth of clothing and jewelry as her husband won the green jacket.Rory, meanwhile, rocked a $100,000 rose gold Omega de ville rose tourbillon watch as he put on the green jacket.The Masters champion thanked his family for their supportMcIlroy gave a lot of praise to his wife and family for their support during his run at The Masters.\"Thank you first and foremost my wife and daughter, Erica and Poppy,\" he said.\"They have to put up with me at home and trust me, sometimes that's a tough thing to do. But they have been my biggest supporters.\"McIlroy has now made more than $110 million in PGA Tour earnings throughout his career. He's likely made several hundred million more through endorsements, investments and more.This story was originally published by The Spun on Apr 14, 2026, where it first appeared in the Golf section. Add The Spun as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
